{"count": 2358, "header": "Found 2358 declarations mentioning Nat.Prime.\nOf these, only the first 200 are shown.\n", "heartbeats": 23, "hits": [{"doc": "`Nat.Prime p` means that `p` is a prime number, that is, a natural number\nat least 2 whose only divisors are `p` and `1`.\nThe theorem `Nat.prime_def` witnesses this description of a prime number.", "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.Prime", "type": " (p : ℕ) : Prop"}, {"doc": "This instance is set up to work in the kernel (`by decide`) for small values.\n\nBelow (`decidablePrime'`) we will define a faster variant to be used by the compiler\n(e.g. in `#eval` or `by native_decide`).\n\nIf you need to prove that a particular number is prime, in any case\nyou should not use `by decide`, but rather `by norm_num`, which is\nmuch faster.", "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.decidablePrime", "type": " (p : ℕ) : Decidable (Nat.Prime p)"}, {"doc": "This definition is faster in the virtual machine than `decidablePrime`,\nbut slower in the kernel.", "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.decidablePrime'", "type": " (p : ℕ) : Decidable (Nat.Prime p)"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_eleven", "type": " : Nat.Prime 11"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_five", "type": " : Nat.Prime 5"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_seven", "type": " : Nat.Prime 7"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_three", "type": " : Nat.Prime 3"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_two", "type": " : Nat.Prime 2"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.decidablePrime_csimp", "type": " : Nat.decidablePrime = Nat.decidablePrime'"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.fact_prime_three", "type": " : Fact (Nat.Prime 3)"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.fact_prime_two", "type": " : Fact (Nat.Prime 2)"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.not_prime_one", "type": " : ¬Nat.Prime 1"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.not_prime_zero", "type": " : ¬Nat.Prime 0"}, {"doc": "A copy of `not_prime_one` stated in a way that works for `aesop`.\n\nSee https://github.com/leanprover-community/aesop/issues/197 for an explanation.", "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_one_false", "type": " : Nat.Prime 1 → False"}, {"doc": "A copy of `not_prime_zero` stated in a way that works for `aesop`.\n\nSee https://github.com/leanprover-community/aesop/issues/197 for an explanation.", "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_zero_false", "type": " : Nat.Prime 0 → False"}, {"doc": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `Nat.prime_iff`.", "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Prime.nat_prime", "type": " {p : ℕ} : Prime p → Nat.Prime p"}, {"doc": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `Nat.prime_iff`.", "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.Prime.prime", "type": " {p : ℕ} : Nat.Prime p → Prime p"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.irreducible_iff_nat_prime", "type": " (a : ℕ) : Irreducible a ↔ Nat.Prime a"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.prime_iff", "type": " {p : ℕ} : Nat.Prime p ↔ Prime p"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.Prime.minFac_eq", "type": " {p : ℕ} (hp : Nat.Prime p) : p.minFac = p"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.Prime.ne_one", "type": " {p : ℕ} (hp : Nat.Prime p) : p ≠ 1"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.Prime.ne_zero", "type": " {n : ℕ} (h : Nat.Prime n) : n ≠ 0"}, {"doc": null, "module": "Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs", "name": "Nat.minFac_prime", "type": " {n : ℕ} (n1 : n ≠